{"id":"polynomial_kernel","title":"Polynomial kernel","family":"kernel","definition":"reference","intro_en":"The polynomial kernel first computes an inner product, then applies a shifted integer power. Here degree three creates nonlinear interactions implicitly without constructing every product feature. The animation separates the coordinate sum from its nonlinear expansion, so the large final magnitude is not mistaken for a probability.","intro_zh":"多项式核先计算内积，再对平移后的结果取整数次幂。本例次数为三，隐式表示非线性交互而不逐一构造乘积特征。动图分开显示坐标求和与非线性展开，最终大数值不能解释为概率。","steps_en":["Use the same aligned coordinate system for both vectors.","Compute and sum the coordinatewise contributions shown in the plot.","Apply the specified scalar kernel transformation to that complete sum.","Read the pair score; kernel magnitude is not a calibrated similarity probability."],"steps_zh":["对两个向量使用同一个已对齐坐标系。","计算图示逐坐标贡献并求和。","对完整求和结果施加指定的标量核变换。","读取成对分数；核函数量级不是校准后的相似概率。"],"formula":"K(x,y)=(0.1*dot(x,y)+1)^3","caveats_en":["The usual positive-semidefinite guarantee uses a nonnegative scale/offset and integer degree. Large norms or degrees can dominate numerically.","No local time warping is performed by this aligned-vector construction."],"caveats_zh":["通常的半正定保证使用非负尺度、非负偏置和整数次数；较大范数或次数可能在数值上主导结果。","此已对齐向量构造不执行局部时间扭曲。"],"sources":[{"label":"scikit-learn: pairwise kernels and their formulas","url":"https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/metrics.html"}],"x":[0.2,0.4,1.1,2.4,3.2,2.5,1.2,0.3,-0.4,-0.1],"y":[0.1,0.3,0.5,1.2,2.6,3.1,2.3,1.1,0.2,-0.3],"input_label":"Deterministic illustrative arrays; no benchmark data","parameters":{"preprocessing":"none","gamma":0.1,"coef0":1.0,"degree":3},"result":{"label":"kernel score","value":34.90166483200001,"detail":"The explicit definition and parameters shown on this card."},"frames":[{"phase":0,"caption":"Compute the indicated contribution at each aligned index","panel":{"kind":"bars","title":"Coordinate products","a":[0.020000000000000004,0.12],"labels":["1","2"],"marker":1,"a_la